			"primaryType": "pizza_restaurant",
			"shortFormattedAddress": "148 Bedford Ave, Brooklyn",
			"editorialSummary": {
				"text": "Bedford Avenue pizza fixture serving up exotic slices & vegan options from a modest counter.",
				"languageCode": "en"
			},
			"reviews": [
				{
					"name": "places/ChIJbSt7rF1ZwokRrnJ-xbOu0i4/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25vMFlsZ3daRkJNWjNaQlZIVTJjbWc1TVVkbVFsRRAB",
					"relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago",
					"rating": 5,
					"text": {
						"text": "Definitely worth a visit if you're in the Williamsburg area. No matter which slice you get, each has that beautiful undercarriage with perfect cheese to sauce ratio. They even offer vegan slices which not many slice shops offer. The staff is quick but very courteous. Interior is loud but it's that lively friendly kind.\n\nOverall just a great pizza joint.",
						"languageCode": "en"
					},
					"originalText": {
						"text": "Definitely worth a visit if you're in the Williamsburg area. No matter which slice you get, each has that beautiful undercarriage with perfect cheese to sauce ratio. They even offer vegan slices which not many slice shops offer. The staff is quick but very courteous. Interior is loud but it's that lively friendly kind.\n\nOverall just a great pizza joint.",
						"languageCode": "en"
					},
					"authorAttribution": {
